  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund for Resilient Ukraine (PFRU) 2022-2025 - Partnership Fund for Resilient Ukraine</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Partnerskapsfond f&#xf6;r motst&#xe5;ndskraftiga Ukraina 2022-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Fonden har utformats i samarbete med Ukrainas regering (GoU) och deltagande finansieringspartners med utg&#xe5;ngspunkt i internationella bevis f&#xf6;r stabiliseringsprogrammering och forskning som bedrivs specifikt f&#xf6;r sammanhanget i Ukraina. Analysen av konflikten, orsakad av Ryska federationens v&#xe4;pnade aggression, har visat att PFRU kan st&#xf6;dja Ukraina f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka motst&#xe5;ndskraften p&#xe5; flera omr&#xe5;den: att mildra effekterna av hybridteknik som Ryssland antagit f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja instabilitet i Ukraina; att st&#xf6;dja Ukraina n&#xe4;r det g&#xe4;ller att ta itu med drivkrafterna till instabilitet i GCA i Donetsk och Luhansk och andra &#xf6;stra och s&#xf6;dra oblaster. och att f&#xf6;rbereda konfliktdrabbade samh&#xe4;llen f&#xf6;r eventuell &#xe5;terintegrering av NGCA: er n&#xe4;r en politisk l&#xf6;sning har uppn&#xe5;tts.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PFRU has been designed collaboratively with the Government of Ukraine (GoU) and participating financing partners drawing on international evidence on stabilisation programming, and research conducted specific to the context in Ukraine. The analysis of the conflict, caused by the armed aggression of the Russian Federation, has indicated that the PFRU can support Ukraine to strengthen resilience in several areas: to mitigate the impact of hybrid tactics adopted by Russia to foment instability in Ukraine; to support Ukraine in addressing the drivers of instability in GCAs of Donetsk and Luhansk and other eastern and southern oblasts; and to prepare conflict-affected communities for the eventual reintegration of NGCAs once a political settlement is achieved.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed contribution &quot;Partnership Fund for Resilient Ukraine&quot; (PFRU) aims to
support Ukrainian Government and citizens to combat consequences of the ongoing
military war in Ukraine provoked by the Russian Federation, as well as to strengthen
resilience of Ukraine towards internal and external threats leading to the destabilization
in Ukraine.

The primary objectives of the PFRU programme are as follows:
- Ukraine&apos;s resilience to instability and conflict is strengthened and Ukraine is prepared
for a smooth social, economic and political transition once there is a political settlement
to the conflictQ
- Ukraine is supported to prevent new conflicts and mitigate instability in Government
Controlled Areas (GCAs) in eastern and southern Ukraine, and to prepare for social,
economic and political reintegration of Non-Government Controlled Areas (NGCAs).

The PFRU will deliver technical support, capacity building and projects (including
infrastructure and construction projects), to support Ukraine to resist the Russian
invasion, mitigate the consequences of the war and possible drivers of instability in the
future and prepare for the reintegration of non-government controlled areas (NGCAs).
This will be provided in close partnership with central and local government
empowering ongoing reforms, in particular decentralisation.</narrative>
  </description>
